Subject: [PATCH] Name the private config layer in the daemon identity; let unreadable RE inputs fail only RE use

Base: facebook/buck2 9a1876786f32806f6b65fc51f4c1c3077efc38a5 plus the
preceding Sekka patches.

The daemon reads BUCK2_EXTRA_EXTERNAL_CONFIG from its own environment,
but the startup identity covered only a digest of [buck2_re_client]. A
client naming another private layer with the same RE settings kept the
old daemon and its old layer. The layer's path now joins the identity.

The digest also failed every command, local-only ones included, when a
[buck2_re_client] value named an unset environment variable or a TLS
file that could not be read. Upstream fails only when the RE client is
built. Such inputs now add a marker to the digest instead, so fixing
them later still restarts the daemon.

